---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolPageFrame from '../components/ImageToolPageFrame.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { GEMINI_AI_LOGO_REMOVER_TOOL } from '../config/image-tools';
import { GEMINI_AI_LOGO_REMOVER_FAQ } from '../content/gemini-ai-logo-remover-faq';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
const tool = GEMINI_AI_LOGO_REMOVER_TOOL;
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'ConvertAnyFile Gemini AI Logo Remover', url: `${SITE.origin}/gemini-ai-logo-remover/`, applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  featureList: ['Local browser processing','Manual Circle mask','Manual 4-Point Star mask','Move, resize and rotate masks','Automatic shared or individual editing recommendation','Mixed aspect-ratio batch support','Separate per-image masks','Up to 50 images per batch','10 MB per source image','Cancelable sequential processing','ZIP download','JPG, PNG and WebP input','No image upload'],
};
---
<SiteLayout title={tool.title} description={tool.description} schema={schema}>
  <ImageToolPageFrame tool={tool} />
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Focused two-shape workflow</span><h2>Use only the shapes that make sense for a small sparkle-style badge.</h2><p>Gemini AI Logo Remover intentionally keeps the toolbar simple: Circle and 4-Point Star. The star is the default. Circle is useful when the visible glow is rounder than the bright core.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>No logo Auto Select</strong><p>You place the mask yourself. The editor only recommends whether the batch should share one mask or keep separate masks based on the uploaded layouts.</p></div></div><ul class="content-checklist"><li>Add one image or up to 50 JPG, PNG, or WebP images, with a 10 MB per-image limit.</li><li>Matching aspect ratios default to One mask for all for repeated placement.</li><li>Mixed aspect ratios stay in the batch and default to Edit individually.</li><li>Move, resize, and rotate Circle or 4-Point Star masks; individual images can keep custom overrides.</li><li>Cancel a long batch and keep results that already completed.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">How it works</span><h2>Four steps from upload to repaired images.</h2><p>The browser recommends a starting editing mode, but the visible-logo mask stays under your control.</p></div><div class="steps-grid"><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Add your image or batch</h3><p>Add one image or up to 50. Mixed aspect ratios are allowed; unsupported or oversized files are rejected independently.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Use the recommended mode</h3><p>Same-ratio batches start with One mask for all. Mixed-ratio batches start with Edit individually. Switch the toggle whenever you prefer.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Fit Circle or 4-Point Star</h3><p>Place the mask over the visible badge, drag inside it to move, use a square corner handle to resize, or drag the round handle to rotate. Processing stays local and sequential.</p></article><article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">04</span><h3>Review and download</h3><p>Click a processed thumbnail to restore its After preview. Use source format, PNG, JPG, or WebP; multiple successful results download as ZIP.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Circle or star</span><h2>Choose the smallest mask that covers the visible badge.</h2><p>A tighter mask leaves more nearby pixels untouched for the local repair algorithm. The 4-Point Star follows a sparkle-like footprint; Circle is useful when the badge includes a compact rounded glow. Rotation helps when the badge itself is tilted.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Shared mask is about placement</strong><p>Matching aspect ratio helps, but the logo should also remain at the same relative position, angle, and approximate size. If it moves or rotates between images, use individual editing.</p></div></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Selection</th><th>Use it when</th><th>Trade-off</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Circle</strong></td><td>The visible badge or glow is approximately round.</td><td>May include extra pixels around long sparkle tips.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4-Point Star</strong></td><td>The badge has a four-point sparkle footprint.</td><td>Needs careful sizing when the glow extends beyond the bright core.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Visible pixels only</span><h2>This is not an invisible-provenance remover.</h2><p>The tool changes visible pixels inside the mask you choose. It does not claim to detect or remove Content Credentials, metadata, invisible watermark systems, provenance signals, authenticity systems, or SynthID-style signals.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Independent product</strong><p>ConvertAnyFile is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google or Gemini. The name is used descriptively for this visible-logo editing workflow.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><FaqList items={GEMINI_AI_LOGO_REMOVER_FAQ} title="Gemini AI Logo Remover FAQ" intro="Circle and four-point-star selection, move/resize/rotate interaction, shared or individual masks, mixed-ratio batches, local repair, cancelable processing, and visible-pixel limitations." /></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Related Image Tools</span><h2>Use Remove Watermark when the mark needs a broader mask vocabulary.</h2><p>The general editor uses the same batch runtime but adds Rectangle, Square, Diamond, Circle, 4-Point Star, and a manual text-shaped mask.</p></div><ImageToolGrid compact /></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
